  "causes": [
    "The shared presentation scaler treated Forest Heart as a legacy DOM game and capped its iframe at 1120 CSS pixels. The reported-size regression reproduced 1021 unused pixels.",
    "The character image kept its aspect ratio at the bottom of a narrow, tall box, pushing its visible head below the field.",
    "Moving the character back from the mobile status row prepended it before the field, swapping implicit grid columns on a return to desktop."
  ],
  "changes": [
    "The shared host delegates sizing to the Forest Heart iframe, as for other independently sized games.",
    "The square field and full-height character are fitted together inside the actual stage; wide grid columns are explicit.",
    "Short landscape windows use a control rail beside the field, with the free action and bonus progress visible.",
    "The game retains its connected chat on desktop, phones and tablets; tall tablet scenes use an intentional upper-body banner."
  ],
